<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Watergate scandal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1972–1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Watergate scandal was a political scandal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> that began with a break-in at the Democratic Party headquarters in the Watergate complex in Washington in June 1972 by men linked to President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon">Richard Nixon</a>'s re-election campaign. Nixon's part in the cover-up, revealed by secret tape recordings, led him to resign in August 1974 to avoid impeachment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/watergate-scandal.jpg" alt="Watergate scandal" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Watergate_complex.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
